---
import Cursor from "@components/cursor.astro";
import Footer from "@components/footer.astro";
import Header from "@components/header.astro";
import Meta from "@components/meta.astro";
import Scripts from "@components/scripts.astro";
---

<html>
<head>
    <Meta name="Services"
          description="Check out my list of self-hosted services, including GitLab, Sharkey and Uptime-Kuma! :3" />
    <Scripts />
    <Cursor />
    <style>
        .error {
            background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgb(136, 0, 0) 20%, rgb(78, 0, 0) 50%, rgb(150, 1, 1) 100%);
            color: white;
            border: 2px solid red;
            padding: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
<canvas id="background"></canvas>
<!-- God damnit, I'm forced to use inline styles because Astro is stupid -->
<div style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;">
    <Header />
    <main>
        <br>
        <div class="error">
            <span>
                <strong>Note:</strong>
                <span>Running these services isn't free. If you have spare money, please <a href="/donate">donate</a>. Thank you!</span>
            </span>
        </div>
        <h1>Self-hosted services</h1>
        <p>
            I recently (2024/10/28) started self hosting a few pieces of software for my own use. Most of these services
            have registrations enabled, although registrations require approval. Here are some of my picks for what I
            host:
        </p>

        <h2>Akabot: My Own Discord Bot</h2>
        <p>I maintain and run my own Discord bot. More on that is available <a href="/project/akabot">in its project
            page</a>.</p>
        <p>There are 2 versions of Akabot that are run on my server. One is the public version and the other is the beta
            version.</p>

        <h2>Forgejo: Git server</h2>
        <p>
            I self-host an instance of Forgejo for my personal use. I host all of my code on it, mirroring it to other services and I also host mirrors of some of my favorite services.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <a href="https://git.lunya.pet/Lunya">https://git.lunya.pet/Lunya</a> - This is my profile.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://git.lunya.pet/explore">https://git.mldchan.dev/explore</a> - Here you can explore all
                of the public projects on this server.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Sharkey: The Fediverse</h2>
        <p>I picked Sharkey for my Fedi software. It is amazing to use and the FE has a lot of cool features :3</p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <a href="https://social.mldchan.dev/mld">https://social.mldchan.dev/mld</a> - This is my profile.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://social.mldchan.dev/">https://social.mldchan.dev/</a> - This is the main page of the
                software. It looks kinda cool with all the moving stuff, doesn't it? :3
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>GlitchTip: A Sentry Alternative</h2>
        <p>I have GlitchTip running, albeit only for personal use -- I use this to monitor my own software and send
            reports to my own server, where no data is sold and is at my home in a safe place.</p>
        <p>It for example monitors Sharkey, Akabot and GitLab from this list.</p>

        <h1>Fedi Services</h1>

        <p>Fedi services in this section refers to features like bots. This does not include Sharkey, which is listed above.</p>

        <h2>FediMeow: The meowing bot</h2>

        <p>This bot is really simple, it sends a meow every hour.</p>

        <a href="/project/fedi/meow/">
            <button>View project page</button>
        </a>

        <h2>Fedi Streaks: Akabot Chat Streaks, for fedi</h2>

        <p>This bot counts consecutive days of you posting on fedi.</p>

        <a href="/project/fedi/streaks/">
            <button>View project page</button>
        </a>

        <h2>Fedi Summarizer: Akabot Chat Summary, for fedi</h2>

        <p>This bot summarizes the amount of notes you post every midnight.</p>

        <a href="/project/fedi/summarizer/">
            <button>View project page</button>
        </a>

        <h1>Services for friends</h1>

        <h2>Cutie Hangout Bot: A friends only bot for funsies :3</h2>
        <p>This is a Discord bot that connects 2 Minecraft servers, a website and a Discord server together. It shows
            the status of the MC servers in both the Discord and on the website. Users can customize settings on the
            website as well.</p>
        <p>This bot was named after the Discord server in which it is used: Cutie Hangout.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://chb.mldchan.dev">https://chb.mldchan.dev</a> - This shows the status of the 2 Minecraft
                servers.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Crafty: Minecraft dashboard</h2>
        <p>This is a dashboard for managing Minecraft servers. It allows creating, managing, deleting servers, adding
            plugins, deleting plugins, running commands all from one site. This service is only accessible internally
            from the network and not available to the public. I run a MC server for some of my friends.</p>

        <h2>QueerBot: Yet another silly bot</h2>
        <p>This one is less complicated than Cutie Hangout Bot, but it is very silly in it's own way. This bot is very
            obsessed with meowing, and :3.</p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
</div>
<script is:inline defer src="/scripts/background.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
